 initial segment (AIS) of pyramidal cells, with a single cell innervating hundreds of pyramidal cells in a clustered manner. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Chandelier.\")\n30062: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023036 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n30063: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_4023036 \"ILX:0107356\")\n30064: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023036 \"Chandelier PV\")\n30065: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023036 cl:BDS_subset)\n30066: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023036 \"In mice, Chandelier PV cells have soma found in in upper L2/3, with some in deep L5 and exhibit fast-spiking but lower firing rate compared to basket cells, and have practically absent hyperpolarization sag.\")\n30067: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023036 \"chandelier pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron\")\n30068: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 obo:CL_0000099)\n30069: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 obo:CL_4023018)\n30070: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070011))\n30071: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956))\n30072: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n30073: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\n30074: \n30075: # Class: obo:CL_4023038 (L6b glutamatergic cortical neuron)\n30076: \n30077: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023038 \"L6b glut\")\n30078: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2020.10.19.34312\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023038 \"A glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 6b. They are transcriptomically related to corticothalamic-projecting neurons but have differential projections to the thalamus or anterior cingulate.\")\n30079: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023038 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n\n(Showing lines 30050-30079 of 35063. Use offset=30080 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"wikipediaversioned:Ganglionic_eminence&oldid=1186824360\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023035 \"A neuron that is derived from a precursor cell in the lateral ganglion eminence.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023035 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023035 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10377350\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023035 \"LGE-derived neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023035 \"lateral ganglionic eminence derived neuron\"@en)\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023035 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:UBERON_0004025)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023035 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001017))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4023036 (chandelier pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023036 \"chandelier PV interneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023036 \"A transcriptomically distinct pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron that is recognizable by the straight terminal axonal 'cartridges' of vertically oriented strings of synaptic boutons. Chandelier PV cells' boutons target exclusively the axon initial segment (AIS) of pyramidal cells, with a single cell innervating hundreds of pyramidal cells in a clustered manner. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Chandelier.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023036 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_4023036 \"ILX:0107356\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023036 \"Chandelier PV\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_4023036 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023036 \"In mice, Chandelier PV cells have soma found in in upper L2/3, with some in deep L5 and exhibit fast-spiking but lower firing rate compared to basket cells, and have practically absent hyperpolarization sag.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023036 \"chandelier pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 obo:CL_0000099)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 obo:CL_4023018)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778376281128,"end":1778376281180}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08d030973c6e72c30169ffde5915308190851010181493660d"}},"id":"prt_e0f7c8c1f001rylnyXcsYa7M9g","sessionID":"ses_1f083bab2ffeWT5rFxWCvS4E20","messageID":"msg_e0f7c7b82001uiTKUKhjGx6LD8"}}
