{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778376323666,"sessionID":"ses_1f083bab2ffeWT5rFxWCvS4E20","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_GUTN5GX3yye3spMTrpXFGKZf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"CLM_100008|Chandelier|chandelier","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","include":"cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 15 matches\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 30058: # Class: obo:CL_4023036 (chandelier pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron)\n\n  Line 30060: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023036 \"chandelier PV interneuron\")\n\n  Line 30061: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023036 \"A transcriptomically distinct pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron that is recognizable by the straight terminal axonal 'cartridges' of vertically oriented strings of synaptic boutons. Chandelier PV cells' boutons target exclusively the axon initial segment (AIS) of pyramidal cells, with a single cell innervating hundreds of pyramidal cells in a clustered manner. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Chandelier.\")\n\n  Line 30064: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023036 \"Chandelier PV\")\n\n  Line 30066: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023036 \"In mice, Chandelier PV cells have soma found in in upper L2/3, with some in deep L5 and exhibit fast-spiking but lower firing rate compared to basket cells, and have practically absent hyperpolarization sag.\")\n\n  Line 30067: Annota